  <h2 id="answer">The direct answer: teaching is the floor, ownership is the ceiling</h2>

  <p>
    Search results on career options in physical education mostly list a dozen job titles with entry salaries. They rarely say that most of these posts have fixed pay, that the best-paid routes need business skills the course does not teach, or that getting a post is a separate contest from getting the degree.
  </p>

  <p>
    A better order is the subject and the degree first, then the options ranked by how far they can grow, then pay with its source, then the competition, and last the sales skills that decide whether a coach earns a salary or a business.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--amber">
    <p class="callout__eyebrow">Questions students actually ask</p>
    <ul class="callout__list">
      <li>"What are the career options in physical education after Class 12?"</li>
      <li>"Is B.P.Ed a good career, or only for teachers?"</li>
      <li>"Can I get a government job with B.P.Ed?"</li>
      <li>"What do I write for career options in physical education in Class 11?"</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="callout__footer">
      Short answers: teaching, coaching, fitness, sports management and analysis; it is more than teaching but the teaching posts are the steadiest; yes, through separate notices; and the Class 11 answer is in the next section.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="class11">Physical education as a Class 11-12 subject</h2>

  <p>
    CBSE physical education (code 048) is a 100-mark subject: 70 marks of theory across ten units, and 30 of practical. Unit 1, Changing Trends and Careers in Physical Education, covers the career groups, and the course also covers Khelo India and Fit India. The practical marks cover a fitness test, games proficiency, yoga, a record file and a viva. Read the current syllabus on the <a href="https://www.cbseacademic.nic.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CBSE academic site</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--gold">
    <p><strong>A short answer you can write in an exam:</strong></p>
    <p>
      Career options in physical education include teaching (physical education teacher), coaching (sports coach, fitness trainer), sports management (event coordinator, sports administrator), health and fitness (personal trainer, wellness coach), sports media (journalist, analyst) and rehabilitation support through further study. A coach trains players to improve skill, fitness and performance, usually after playing experience and a diploma or degree in physical education.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    The subject helps if you enjoy it, since it builds practical fitness and sports knowledge. It is not a gate. Graduates in any discipline can apply for B.P.Ed, so a student in any stream can reach this career later. If you are in humanities, see <a href="/blog/career-options/career-options-after-12th-humanities/">career options after 12th humanities</a> for how this sits beside law, design and teaching.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ladder">The degree ladder: B.P.Ed, M.P.Ed and UGC NET</h2>

  <p>
    Each step below unlocks a different set of posts. Exam bodies and universities revise rules, so confirm on the official page before you pay a fee.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Step</th>
          <th>What the rules say</th>
          <th>What it unlocks</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
