          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">
    Official sources: <a href="https://igipess.du.ac.in/Admission-Procedure.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Delhi University's IGIPESS admission page</a> (B.Sc, B.P.Ed and M.P.Ed), <a href="https://ncte.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NCTE</a> for teacher-education rules, <a href="https://ugcnet.nta.nic.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NTA's UGC NET portal</a>, and <a href="https://www.lnipe.edu.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LNIPE</a> for its two campuses. The NCTE 2014 change from one year to two is taken from university notices that quote the regulation. LNIPE's entrance route was described differently on different sites, so read its prospectus.
  </p>

  <p>
    For performance-science routes such as strength and conditioning, biomechanics and the national coaching diploma, read <a href="/blog/career-options/exercise-science-career-options/">exercise science career options</a>. This page stays with the physical education subject and the teaching, coaching and ownership routes around it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="options">The career options, ordered by headroom</h2>

  <p>
    The order is not prestige and not exam difficulty. Routes that can grow through ownership, repeat clients or a portfolio come first, because they give you more choices later. Every route carries a scalability rating and its catch.
  </p>

  <div class="proof-grid">
    {optionCards.map((item) => (
      <div class="proof-card path-card">
        <span class="proof-card__track">{item.badge}</span>
        <p><strong>{item.title}.</strong> {item.body}</p>
